From 6e0357ded90b80de2b383db7e80f70412da2b2be Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Philipp Bogdan <174341097+philippbogdan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 03:28:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] correlation groups: analytic counting noise by default; data
 sets without usable pairs not judged; pairs need p < 0.001

- noise_model=analytic (default): the counting noise of every pairwise correlation is the
  large-sample error of Fisher's z with the pair's effective number of reflections (the
  quantity cosym keeps as its weight), drawn independently for every pair. Measured against
  repeat measurements of the same crystals (disjoint rotation ranges), it is within a factor
  0.6-1.4 of the truth where the bootstrap over reflections overstates the noise 1.5-5 fold
  (pairs sharing few reflections); and it costs no recomputation of the correlations.
  noise_model=bootstrap keeps the previous model.
- A correlation without noise of its own (too few reflections for an error) is left out of
  the scan; data sets with fewer than min_usable_pairs such correlations are not judged.
- pair_significance (default 0.001): a group of two data sets needs stronger evidence
  against counting noise.
- Tests for the analytic noise, the effective numbers of reflections, the unjudged data
  sets and the pair threshold.
